      {
        "id": 2563482,
        "name": "Sasha Nemtsov",
        "username": "Sasha_Nemtsov",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/sasha_nemtsov/{size}/393707_2.png",
        "created_at": "2024-07-17T13:43:52.003Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There’s a misunderstanding linked to the previous reply to you.</p>\n<p>Botting is the use of scripts to automate certain functions in a game. A ‘botter’ does not have to be physically present in order for his characters to perform their assigned tasks. I think this is used mainly in mining, but anyone can correct me if I’m wrong.</p>\n<p>Input Broadcasting and allied functions also allow a player to automate certain operations in the game, but the player must be present at the keyboard in order to (at least) initiate the activity.</p>\n<p>Both botting and input broadcasting are prohibited, and most players are perfectly aware of this without reading the Eula, etc.</p>\n<p>There are allowed means of controlling multiple characters. So, to answer your questions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Botting is illegal, full stop. If people are ‘getting away with it’, it’s only because they haven’t (yet) been caught. It is rather a game of ‘catch-up’ though, for CCP.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>There are no permitted means of simultaneously performing <em>automated</em> actions involving multiple characters, apart from those already present in the game (e.g. ore moves automatically to the ore hold of a barge, fleet-warp, etc.).</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>I think your thread and its title are disingenuous. It is a back-handed invitation to thrash out yet again a perceived indifference to the issue of botting by the Company. I reject this.</p>\n<p>You posted in New Citizens Q&amp;A, which is designed to offer help to those just starting out with the game. Surely, botting and input broadcasting would be well down their list of priorities at that stage?</p>\n<p>Troll thread, therefore. I only replied because you posted in this sub-forum. If you’d put it in GD, where it belongs, I’d have ignored it completely.</p>",
